d":"W3139453502","year":2021},{"abstract":"","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5048754844","A5080941020","A5082103014","A5085789605","A5100421891","A5102218122"],"author_institution_ids":["I1174212"],"authors":[{"id":"A5102218122","name":"LI Ke-tian"},{"id":"A5080941020","name":"Yanchu Zhang"},{"id":"A5085789605","name":"Kunhao Yu"},{"id":"A5082103014","name":"Haixu Du"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"},{"id":"A5100421891","name":"Qiming Wang"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":3,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmps.2024.105661","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I1174212"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Journal of the Mechanics and Physics of Solids","last_updated":"2026-11-11T12:16:26.678958","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"bronze","oa_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0022509624001273","openalex_topics":["T10396","T10753","T12362"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-04-25","study_type":"article","title":"Mechanics of abrasion-induced particulate matter emission","type":"article","work_id":"W4395468817","year":2024},{"abstract":"Recent research highlights that non-exhaust emissions from the abrasion of tires and other organic materials have emerged as a substantial source of airborne particulate matter and marine microplastics. Despite their growing impact, the underlying mechanisms driving these abrasion emissions have remained largely unexplored. In this study, we uncover that abrasion emissions from organic materials are fundamentally governed by a fatigue fracture process, wherein particles are progressively detached from the material surface under cyclic abrasion loads. Our findings demonstrate that these emissions increase significantly only when the applied abrasion loads surpass the material's toughness threshold. We establish a scaling relationship between the concentration of emitted particulate matter and the measurable crack propagation rate of the organic material, offering a robust quantitative method to estimate abrasion emissions. This work not only introduces a novel mechanistic framework for understanding particulate matter pollution from organic material abrasion but also provides a scientific basis for developing strategies to mitigate emissions of airborne particulates and marine microplastics.","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5048754844","A5080941020","A5082103014","A5085789605","A5100421891","A5102218122"],"author_institution_ids":["I1174212"],"authors":[{"id":"A5102218122","name":"LI Ke-tian"},{"id":"A5085789605","name":"Kunhao Yu"},{"id":"A5080941020","name":"Yanchu Zhang"},{"id":"A5082103014","name":"Haixu Du"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"},{"id":"A5100421891","name":"Qiming Wang"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":9,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-74137-6","domain_tags":["air"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air","matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I1174212"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Scientific Reports","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"cc-by-nc-nd","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-74137-6.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10075","T10753","T12095"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-10-10","study_type":"article","title":"Unveiling the mechanism secret of abrasion emissions of particulate matter and microplastics","type":"article","work_id":"W4403298845","year":2024},{"abstract":"","author_count":9,"author_ids":["A5005304188","A5009007394","A5028796505","A5029277426","A5043436376","A5048754844","A5083525391","A5120431484"],"author_institution_ids":["I1174212"],"authors":[{"id":"A5120431484","name":"Sahar Fazelvalipour"},{"id":"A5083525391","name":"Yashar Aghaei"},{"id":"A5029277426","name":"Mohammad Mahdi Badami"},{"id":"A5028796505","name":"Mohammad Aldekheel"},{"id":"A5009007394","name":"Ramin Tohidi"},{"id":"A5005304188","name":"P. S. Ganesh Subramanian"},{"id":"A5043436376","name":"Vishal Verma"},{"id":"","name":"Jiachen Zhang"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":3,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2025.121686","domain_tags":["air"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air"],"institution_ids":["I1174212","I1316958739","I157725225","I36721946"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Atmospheric Environment","last_updated":"2026-09-27T08:07:27.782135","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2025.121686","openalex_topics":["T10075","T10190","T12095"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10075","pub_date":"2025-11-20","study_type":"article","title":"Contributions of tailpipe and non-tailpipe emissions to the oxidative potential of source-resolved PM10 from major LDV- and HDV-dominated freeways in Los Angeles","type":"article","work_id":"W4416418629","year":2025},{"abstract":"","author_count":13,"author_ids":["A5001328363","A5028077050","A5029277426","A5036057349","A5048754844","A5076250081","A5083525391","A5084487425","A5117726111","A5120431484","A5138388453","A5140529446","A5140536228"],"author_institution_ids":["I1174212"],"authors":[{"id":"A5120431484","name":"Sahar Fazelvalipour"},{"id":"A5036057349","name":"Y U E J I He"},{"id":"A5029277426","name":"Mohammad Mahdi Badami"},{"id":"A5117726111","name":"Diego Ramos Aguilera"},{"id":"A5138388453","name":"Venezia Ramirez"},{"id":"A5083525391","name":"Yashar Aghaei"},{"id":"A5001328363","name":"Vahid Jalali Farahani"},{"id":"A5140529446","name":"Yunhan Huang"},{"id":"A5084487425","name":"Mo Chen"},{"id":"A5028077050","name":"Sara D. Forestieri"},{"id":"A5076250081","name":"David C. Quiros"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"},{"id":"A5140536228","name":"Jiachen Zhang"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7114236","domain_tags":["fate_transport_and_sorption"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I1174212"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"SSRN Electronic Journal","last_updated":"2026-11-09T13:22:03.289127","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7114236","openalex_topics":["T10768","T12095","T12126"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T12095","pub_date":"2026-01-01","study_type":"preprint","title":"Forgone Community Emission Benefits in Southern California Without Zero-Emission Truck Regulations","type":"preprint","work_id":"W7168186223","year":2026},{"abstract":"Airborne microplastics (MPs) are increasingly recognized as atmospheric pollutants with potential implications for human exposure; however, their occurrence, temporal variability, and associations with urban particulate matter remain poorly understood. This study investigated MPs associated with PM10 in central Los Angeles across two seasonal sampling campaigns by integrating MP abundance, morphology, size distribution, PM10 chemical composition, and meteorological observations. MPs were detected in all samples, with concentrations ranging from 2.2-4.0 MP/m3 during the cool-season campaign and 2.2-3.4 MP/m3 during the warm-season campaign. Fibers remained the dominant morphology, while particles <100 \u00b5m, particularly the 5-50 \u00b5m and 50-100 \u00b5m fractions, consistently dominated the airborne MP population. Strong positive correlations (generally \u03c1 \u2265 0.79) were observed between total MP concentrations and major crustal (Fe, Si, Mn, Ca, Al, and Mg), traffic-related (Ba, Cu, and Ni), and carbonaceous (OC and EC) tracers, indicating that MPs are closely associated with urban particulate mixtures influenced by resuspension and non-tailpipe traffic emissions. In contrast, short-term meteorological variability showed no consistent relationship with MP concentrations. These findings indicate that airborne MPs are a persistent component of the urban PM10 mixture rather than isolated contaminants, and provide new insight into their sources and behavior in densely populated urban environments.","author_count":8,"author_ids":["A5002529431","A5025419758","A5029277426","A5048754844","A5083525391","A5120431484","A5158027413","A5158057927"],"author_institution_ids":[],"authors":[{"id":"A5120431484","name":"Sahar Fazelvalipour"},{"id":"A5083525391","name":"Yashar Aghaei"},{"id":"A5029277426","name":"Mohammad Mahdi Badami"},{"id":"A5002529431","name":"Kanchana Chandrakanthan"},{"id":"A5025419758","name":"Pierre Herck\u00e8s"},{"id":"A5158057927","name":"Matthew P. Fraser"},{"id":"A5158027413","name":"Jiachen Zhang"},{"id":"A5048754844","name":"Constantinos Sioutas"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202610.0577.v1","domain_tags":["air","occurrence_and_monitoring"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air"],"institution_ids":[],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Preprints.org","last_updated":"2026-11-09T13:22:03.289127","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202610.0577.v1","openalex_topics":["T10075","T10419","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2026-10-08","study_type":"preprint","title":"Size-Resolved Characteristics and Source Influences of Airborne Microplastics in Central Los Angeles","type":"preprint","work_id":"W7221132240","year":2026}]}
